# The test tools of the integration; the test plugin pins Home Assistant itself.
# Renovate keeps this list and the hash-pinned requirements-test.txt current. The
# lock file is compiled with `uv pip compile --python-version=` for the Python of
# the CI, and Renovate compiles it again with the command in its header (see
# .github/renovate-blueprint.json5). The test plugin is pinned: a Home Assistant
# that needs a newer Python fails its update instead of an older Home Assistant
# being chosen.
coverage
hypothesis
mypy
# Home Assistant's own test plugin, which it publishes with each of its releases at
# the same version. An integration that uses Bluetooth asks for its packages with
# pytest-homeassistant[bluetooth].
pytest-homeassistant==2026.11.2
# The plugins of pytest that the test plugin doesn't bring: the coverage of each
# process of pytest-xdist, which scripts/check.sh measures, the time limit of each
# test in pyproject.toml, and the annotations of a failed test in the CI.
pytest-cov
pytest-timeout
pytest-github-actions-annotate-failures
ruff
